6
00:00:13,780 --> 00:00:16,780
[7HD Channel]

7
00:00:16,780 --> 00:00:19,260
[iQIYI]

8
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:22,940
[Present]

9
00:00:23,220 --> 00:00:26,100
♫Where’s that love people are saying?♫

10
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:29,500
♫To always be by each other’s sides♫

11
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:32,580
♫The love that’s willing to sacrifice everything♫

12
00:00:32,580 --> 00:00:35,580
♫Everything even my own life♫

13
00:00:35,580 --> 00:00:39,060
♫Do they really exist? I’d rather not believe it♫

14
00:00:39,060 --> 00:00:42,140
♫I don’t think I’ll ever fall for anyone♫

15
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:45,380
♫Love? I don’t find it interesting♫

16
00:00:45,380 --> 00:00:48,460
♫Sorry about that♫

17
00:00:48,940 --> 00:00:51,500
♫But then who are you?♫

18
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:55,500
♫To make my heart keep fluttering♫

19
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:57,900
♫Please tell me♫

20
00:00:58,140 --> 00:01:01,220
♫What’s happening with my heart?♫

21
00:01:01,220 --> 00:01:04,580
♫It can’t be, why am I feeling this?♫

22
00:01:04,580 --> 00:01:07,660
♫Oh, my heart is pounding so fast♫

23
00:01:07,660 --> 00:01:10,740
♫Time freezes whenever I see you♫

24
00:01:10,740 --> 00:01:14,100
♫I wonder why every time you smile♫

25
00:01:14,100 --> 00:01:17,380
♫Something in your eyes make me go weak♫

26
00:01:17,380 --> 00:01:20,580
♫Oh no, this is real–it’s not a dream♫

27
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:23,460
♫Or is the love that people are saying...♫

28
00:01:23,460 --> 00:01:25,340
♫Is it you?♫

29
00:01:30,220 --> 00:01:32,060
♫Is it you?♫

30
00:01:32,060 --> 00:01:35,620
[Flaming Chains of Love]

31
00:01:35,620 --> 00:01:37,450
[Previously]
I heard you went to the mine yesterday.

32
00:01:37,450 --> 00:01:42,220
You told your sister to count rocks, and even let her work under the sun.

33
00:01:42,220 --> 00:01:44,320
It was just to practise her patience.

34
00:01:44,320 --> 00:01:47,680
By throwing away her bike and letting her walk to work?

35
00:01:47,680 --> 00:01:50,320
You also made her go through all the accounting papers until late at night.

36
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:51,979
Are you sure you didn’t try to pick on her?

37
00:01:52,250 --> 00:01:52,920
Boo!

38
00:01:52,920 --> 00:01:53,750
Shit!

39
00:01:54,520 --> 00:01:58,120
There’s no hole? Did I punch her too hard she’s gone bonkers?

40
00:01:58,120 --> 00:02:02,220
I want you to take Kaphrao with you to the opening of Nam’s new resort.

41
00:02:02,220 --> 00:02:04,050
Why would you want me to take this Gremlin with me?

42
00:02:04,050 --> 00:02:05,250
I don’t want to go!

43
00:02:05,250 --> 00:02:06,850
If you don’t want to go, then that’s all right.

44
00:02:06,850 --> 00:02:10,949
While Fai is away, I’ll be your coach at work instead, okay?

45
00:02:10,949 --> 00:02:14,320
I’ve changed my mind. I’ll take Guinea Pig to Hua Hin too.

46
00:02:36,470 --> 00:02:38,579
Here, freshen up a bit.

47
00:02:44,130 --> 00:02:46,070
Can you stop making a grumpy face?

48
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:49,780
I’m taking you to congratulate my sister, not to a slaughterhouse.

49
00:02:49,780 --> 00:02:51,070
Try to act more human.

50
00:02:52,329 --> 00:02:53,329
But I don’t want to go.

51
00:02:54,370 --> 00:02:56,820
Why did you change your mind and tell Uncle like that?

52
00:02:59,530 --> 00:03:01,530
It’s fun to see someone being grumpy.

53
00:03:02,700 --> 00:03:03,500
Maniac!

54
00:03:07,170 --> 00:03:08,530
I have three older sisters.

55
00:03:09,170 --> 00:03:09,970
Who asked you?

56
00:03:11,330 --> 00:03:17,220
I’m just saying it–so that you won’t do something stupid and embarrass me in front of my sisters.

57
00:03:17,900 --> 00:03:18,700
No need.

58
00:03:19,130 --> 00:03:20,980
Uncle already told me everything.

59
00:03:22,170 --> 00:03:25,870
You probably acted all innocent and sucked up to my dad to pry it out of him.

60
00:03:26,100 --> 00:03:27,900
It’s lucky I decided to drag you out with me.

61
00:03:28,170 --> 00:03:30,400
Otherwise, you’d have had chances to seduce him more.

62
00:03:31,060 --> 00:03:34,180
Seriously, is your brain only full of crap?

63
00:03:34,870 --> 00:03:38,540
I’m telling you for the umpteenth time–I love and respect Uncle like a father!

64
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:41,900
He’s my dad not yours. Stop stealing someone else’s dad.

65
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:44,860
You’re jealous? Are you eight years old or what?

66
00:03:45,300 --> 00:03:47,570
Hey, watch it! I’m older than you.

67
00:03:48,270 --> 00:03:49,070
Why?

68
00:03:49,730 --> 00:03:53,820
It’s true though–can’t you accept it? So childish.

69
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:03,570
Go back to your seat, chauffeur.

70
00:04:06,770 --> 00:04:08,740
Should I just let her walk there?

71
00:04:16,500 --> 00:04:17,660
[Door knocking]

72
00:04:18,370 --> 00:04:22,700
Akanee, why did you allow that girl to go to Hua Hin with Fai?

73
00:04:23,500 --> 00:04:27,330
It's training for work, and also to get to know Fai’s cousins.

74
00:04:28,070 --> 00:04:31,460
That girl is an outsider. Why would you want to introduce her to them?

75
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:38,380
Kaphrao is Fai’s assistant. She’s supposed to know everything so that it’d be easier when they work together.

76
00:04:38,870 --> 00:04:44,220
Really? I think you actually want to introduce her to everyone in your family.

77
00:04:46,470 --> 00:04:48,000
What are you trying to say, Panee?

78
00:04:48,970 --> 00:04:51,700
You’ve always treated Kaphrao as if she were your own child.

79
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:53,220
You’re being nonsense.

80
00:04:54,060 --> 00:04:57,780
I’m just fond of her. I feel pity for her because she’s an orphan.

81
00:04:58,170 --> 00:05:00,860
Don’t be so biased and narrow-minded.

82
00:05:01,730 --> 00:05:07,060
Fine then. You’d better make sure she wouldn’t do anything to hurt my niece.

83
00:05:07,500 --> 00:05:08,980
Or else she’ll pay for it!

84
00:05:27,660 --> 00:05:33,580
[LADARA Resort&Spa]

85
00:05:33,870 --> 00:05:38,740
Please tell the reservation team to recheck all the bookings carefully, especially for those during the high season.

86
00:05:39,220 --> 00:05:39,940
Yes, Boss.

87
00:05:42,900 --> 00:05:44,940
[Fai]: Nam! Lada!

88
00:05:44,970 --> 00:05:46,620
Oh, you’re here?

89
00:05:47,200 --> 00:05:49,580
Congratulations, Sis.

90
00:05:53,170 --> 00:05:56,340
I bought this super-size banquet especially for you.

91
00:05:56,340 --> 00:05:57,400
Thanks a lot.

92
00:05:58,140 --> 00:06:02,180
May your new business grow and make you a thousand times richer.

93
00:06:03,470 --> 00:06:05,330
But maybe not as rich as Young Master Fai.

94
00:06:05,900 --> 00:06:08,500
Uncle Ak owns a lot more businesses than I do.

95
00:06:08,500 --> 00:06:16,100
Well, he might have plenty but many of his side pieces are also trying to get their hands on his money.

96
00:06:18,970 --> 00:06:20,660
Let me help you with that, Nam.

97
00:06:20,670 --> 00:06:21,470
[Nam]: Careful, it’s heavy.

98
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:24,820
Excuse me, can you put this in her office?

99
00:06:24,820 --> 00:06:26,220
[Staff]: Yes, Boss.
[Lada]: Thank you.

100
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:37,260
This is the Guinea Pig–I mean, Athittaya. You can call her Kaphrao.

101
00:06:37,740 --> 00:06:39,740
She’s one of Dad’s kept women.

102
00:06:42,180 --> 00:06:44,540
She just graduated so he wants her to help with work.

103
00:06:46,460 --> 00:06:49,300
This is my sister, Nam–and my sister-in-law, Lada.

104
00:06:51,900 --> 00:06:54,980
Hello, Miss Nam and Miss Lada.

105
00:07:00,170 --> 00:07:02,860
You’ve come all the way here, why don’t you stay a bit longer?

106
00:07:03,070 --> 00:07:07,000
I have to leave the day after tomorrow. I’m worried about work.

107
00:07:08,970 --> 00:07:12,020
What? Since when have you started to worry about work?

108
00:07:14,100 --> 00:07:16,500
So, where are Din, Lom, and the others?

109
00:07:17,700 --> 00:07:19,500
Din and Rose already arrived.

110
00:07:19,820 --> 00:07:24,260
But Lom and Miss Blew are still in Madelin–they couldn’t make it in time.

111
00:07:24,770 --> 00:07:29,860
Geez, I thought the Watinwanich sisters would be all present this time.

112
00:07:37,780 --> 00:07:38,700
Well…

113
00:07:40,100 --> 00:07:42,420
You must be tired from a long drive.

114
00:07:42,740 --> 00:07:44,580
Let me show you to your room.

115
00:07:44,580 --> 00:07:46,980
[Fai]: Give me your biggest room.
- [Nam]: I know.

116
00:07:49,470 --> 00:07:52,020
Let’s go. Do you like it here?

117
00:07:52,300 --> 00:07:53,540
It’s wonderful.

118
00:08:10,070 --> 00:08:11,420
Guinea Pig!

119
00:08:15,370 --> 00:08:19,140
Hurry up and get changed. My sisters and I will go out for dinner.

120
00:08:19,370 --> 00:08:20,420
I’m not going.

121
00:08:20,700 --> 00:08:24,980
You can go and spend time with your Watinwanich family all you like.

122
00:08:25,170 --> 00:08:27,860
My sisters told me to invite you. Or else, I wouldn’t have asked.

123
00:08:28,100 --> 00:08:29,460
But I don’t know any of them.

124
00:08:29,570 --> 00:08:31,580
You already met Nam and Lada.

125
00:08:35,700 --> 00:08:40,220
If you don’t go, I’ll tell Dad that you don’t show my sisters respect.

126
00:08:41,169 --> 00:08:42,780
No manners.

127
00:08:44,070 --> 00:08:47,020
Fine! I’ll go–so that you’ll shut up.

128
00:08:51,870 --> 00:08:52,930
Why are you following me?

129
00:08:53,100 --> 00:08:53,740
I’m afraid you’ll ditch.

130
00:08:53,930 --> 00:08:54,780
You, freak!

131
00:08:54,870 --> 00:08:57,860
Wear something pretty. Don’t dress up like a servant!

132
00:08:57,970 --> 00:08:59,060
Annoying!

133
00:09:10,130 --> 00:09:11,270
[Lada]: Do you like it?

134
00:09:12,130 --> 00:09:13,500
[Din]: It’s splendid.

135
00:09:13,730 --> 00:09:15,180
[Lada]: Wait until you try the food, it’s amazing.

136
00:09:15,860 --> 00:09:17,060
[Rose]: I can’t wait.
- [Fai]: Wow!

137
00:09:17,060 --> 00:09:19,060
The view here is fantastic!

138
00:09:21,670 --> 00:09:23,780
Finally, what took you so long?

139
00:09:24,470 --> 00:09:26,140
Someone’s been dawdling.

140
00:09:31,330 --> 00:09:32,540
Please have a seat.

141
00:09:34,300 --> 00:09:35,420
Thank you.

142
00:09:41,530 --> 00:09:45,300
Is this the girl you told me she came with Fai?

143
00:09:46,200 --> 00:09:47,000
Yes.

144
00:09:48,570 --> 00:09:50,180
I didn’t want her to come with me though.

145
00:09:50,700 --> 00:09:53,260
Dad made me do it.

146
00:10:00,130 --> 00:10:03,420
I’m Rose. And that’s Din.

147
00:10:04,900 --> 00:10:07,620
Hello.

148
00:10:08,270 --> 00:10:11,660
I’m Kaphrao, or you can just call me Phrao.

149
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:12,800
Okay.

150
00:10:13,500 --> 00:10:14,900
You have quite a unique name.

151
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:21,140
And also a very sweet-looking face. Don’t you think so, Din?

152
00:10:21,670 --> 00:10:25,100
I think she looks really cute.

153
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:28,220
Thank you.

154
00:10:30,700 --> 00:10:32,420
Let’s order something then, shall we?

155
00:10:34,270 --> 00:10:35,620
Can we have the menu?

156
00:10:38,530 --> 00:10:39,660
Thank you.

157
00:10:43,800 --> 00:10:46,340
You must be very close to Fai, Miss Phrao.

158
00:10:46,620 --> 00:10:49,980
I don’t usually see her go somewhere with anyone.

159
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:54,380
It’s not like that. Uncle told her to bring me here too.

160
00:10:54,980 --> 00:10:57,260
She didn’t have a choice but to comply.

161
00:11:02,800 --> 00:11:03,820
Weird, isn’t it?

162
00:11:04,700 --> 00:11:08,860
Usually, Fai is so stubborn to Uncle Ak.

163
00:11:09,420 --> 00:11:10,540
She never listens to him.

164
00:11:10,540 --> 00:11:14,340
That’s right. Nam told me Fai and her father always fight.

165
00:11:17,870 --> 00:11:18,780
Isn’t that right?

166
00:11:23,470 --> 00:11:26,400
So, are you and Fai dating, Miss Phrao?

167
00:11:27,200 --> 00:11:28,000
No!

168
00:11:29,330 --> 00:11:30,530
No, Boss Rose!

169
00:11:32,800 --> 00:11:37,300
There’s no way I’d be interested in her. She’s ugly and not even a bit cute.

170
00:11:37,620 --> 00:11:41,180
She also loves to fix things with her fists. Who the hell in their right mind would like her?

171
00:11:41,180 --> 00:11:44,900
Besides, I don’t want anything to do with Dad’s side chick.

172
00:11:45,180 --> 00:11:48,740
I’d rather stay single forever than have this Gremlin as a girlfriend!

173
00:12:10,370 --> 00:12:12,420
Please excuse me, I need to go to the loo.

174
00:12:15,870 --> 00:12:18,300
Too ashamed to listen to it?

175
00:12:43,770 --> 00:12:45,700
What should I order?

176
00:12:47,370 --> 00:12:50,540
Hmm, they have quite a lot on the menu.

177
00:12:51,470 --> 00:12:54,900
Oh, this one looks good, right?

178
00:13:05,500 --> 00:13:09,060
Does she think she’s so good-looking herself? Buffalo Fai!!!

179
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:12,780
I’m sorry! Please don’t mind me.

180
00:13:33,730 --> 00:13:36,540
Aren’t you guys going to eat? They’re all delicious.

181
00:13:43,870 --> 00:13:46,860
Why are you all looking at me like that?

182
00:13:50,900 --> 00:13:53,820
Seriously, you still have no idea?

183
00:13:54,370 --> 00:13:58,220
About what? I don’t like her. Why would I say otherwise?

184
00:14:01,730 --> 00:14:03,420
Then, just keep it to yourself.

185
00:14:04,130 --> 00:14:06,940
You don’t have to be so harsh to her.

186
00:14:07,170 --> 00:14:09,700
What if someone says those things to you, how would you feel?

187
00:14:09,870 --> 00:14:12,330
And don’t you dare argue you were just being blunt.

188
00:14:12,900 --> 00:14:15,060
What you did was nothing but rude.

189
00:14:15,370 --> 00:14:18,900
Did all those words even pass through your brain before they came out of your mouth?

190
00:14:19,800 --> 00:14:21,620
You need to stop doing that, Fai.

191
00:14:25,200 --> 00:14:26,700
Please be more careful with your words.

192
00:14:26,700 --> 00:14:29,380
Once spoken, they cannot be changed or taken back.

193
00:14:29,380 --> 00:14:32,220
Just like the feelings of the receiving end–already hurt and broken.

194
00:14:39,400 --> 00:14:43,220
Boss Rose, you’re my only hope now.

195
00:14:45,470 --> 00:14:47,460
You understand me, don’t you?

196
00:14:49,900 --> 00:14:51,220
No, I don’t.

197
00:14:52,380 --> 00:14:55,980
I wasn't Miss Phrao but even I felt so hurt and taken aback.

198
00:14:56,220 --> 00:14:58,380
No one on earth would like it.

199
00:14:59,180 --> 00:15:03,460
No wonder why you’re still single.

200
00:15:04,770 --> 00:15:09,180
And if you like her but don’t know how to say it so you just keep picking on her–that’s so outdated.

201
00:15:09,900 --> 00:15:12,020
If she says she hates you, then she means it.

202
00:15:12,330 --> 00:15:13,900
Lada, maybe–

203
00:15:13,900 --> 00:15:15,460
Don’t try to stop me.

204
00:15:15,500 --> 00:15:19,380
It’s because you never give her a serious reprimand,
that’s why she never grows up.

205
00:15:22,070 --> 00:15:25,460
If you ever say something like that to me, I’d definitely break up with you.

206
00:15:32,600 --> 00:15:34,580
You guys are ganging up on me.

207
00:15:34,770 --> 00:15:36,180
I’m out of here.

208
00:15:37,970 --> 00:15:39,740
My ears have gone numb.

209
00:15:48,800 --> 00:15:50,460
Good job, Lada.

210
00:16:24,100 --> 00:16:25,420
Silly Gremlin.

211
00:16:30,260 --> 00:16:31,660
[Door knocking]

212
00:16:31,930 --> 00:16:34,700
Go away! I’m not your bloody Gremlin!

213
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:36,600
S…Sorry.

214
00:16:50,700 --> 00:16:52,100
Where are you going, lady?

215
00:16:53,570 --> 00:16:55,180
Are you in a hurry?

216
00:16:56,900 --> 00:16:58,060
What’s your name?

217
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:01,140
Hey, what the hell!

218
00:17:01,140 --> 00:17:02,780
Get off me!

219
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:04,130
You like it tough, huh?

220
00:17:04,329 --> 00:17:05,599
Quite stubborn, aren’t you?

221
00:17:05,619 --> 00:17:06,460
Let me go!

222
00:17:06,460 --> 00:17:10,260
Hey! Can’t you see she doesn’t want to talk to you?

223
00:17:10,270 --> 00:17:11,380
Fai!

224
00:17:11,400 --> 00:17:12,780
Wanna have fun too, huh?

225
00:17:13,730 --> 00:17:15,420
Have fun, my foot!

226
00:17:18,800 --> 00:17:21,300
Smart mouth, aren’t you? What’s your name, girl?

227
00:17:22,900 --> 00:17:24,780
Go ask your mother then!

228
00:17:25,200 --> 00:17:26,670
Hey! I asked you nicely!

229
00:17:28,700 --> 00:17:32,860
I’ll count ‘one, two…’

230
00:17:34,870 --> 00:17:41,460
[Younger Fai]: I’ll count ‘one, two…’ After three, just run.

231
00:17:54,100 --> 00:17:55,260
[Kaphrao’s crying]

232
00:17:55,260 --> 00:17:56,580
[Fai]: Get off me!

233
00:17:56,700 --> 00:17:59,180
[Kaphrao]: Fai, I’m scared!

234
00:17:59,800 --> 00:18:01,370
Don’t you want a doll?

235
00:18:01,530 --> 00:18:03,540
I’m taking you to get it.

236
00:18:03,660 --> 00:18:06,980
I don’t want it anymore. I’m scared!

237
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:11,420
If you don’t stop crying, I’ll leave you here alone.

238
00:18:12,300 --> 00:18:14,620
Fai, don’t leave me!

239
00:18:18,260 --> 00:18:20,260
[Screaming]

240
00:18:22,370 --> 00:18:27,860
Fai! Please don’t leave me, Fai!

241
00:18:28,370 --> 00:18:29,580
Fai!

242
00:18:29,580 --> 00:18:30,860
[Crying]

243
00:18:32,620 --> 00:18:33,940
Fai..

244
00:18:35,940 --> 00:18:36,700
Let's go.

245
00:19:03,870 --> 00:19:10,460
I’ll count ‘One, two…’ After three, just run, okay?

246
00:19:10,700 --> 00:19:12,500
I can’t run.

247
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:16,800
One.

248
00:19:19,170 --> 00:19:19,970
Two.

249
00:19:22,500 --> 00:19:23,180
Three!

250
00:19:23,180 --> 00:19:24,420
[Screaming]

251
00:19:26,670 --> 00:19:30,900
Three!

252
00:19:31,370 --> 00:19:32,270
Go after them!

253
00:19:37,940 --> 00:19:41,180
Hurry up! Faster!

254
00:19:41,660 --> 00:19:46,740
Out of the way! Damn it!

255
00:19:47,820 --> 00:19:52,700
- Boo!
- [Screaming]

256
00:20:12,940 --> 00:20:16,220
[Panting]

257
00:20:21,800 --> 00:20:23,300
We’ve probably lost them.

258
00:20:23,770 --> 00:20:24,800
They’re that drunk.

259
00:20:32,870 --> 00:20:34,780
I didn’t expect you’d help.

260
00:20:36,870 --> 00:20:38,100
I didn’t mean to.

261
00:20:40,730 --> 00:20:44,460
I only did what any good person would do in that situation.

262
00:20:46,270 --> 00:20:49,600
And I thought you would start throwing punches at them.

263
00:20:50,380 --> 00:20:55,470
Are you nuts? I’m not that stupid. It’s 3:1, I would’ve got myself buried under their feet.

264
00:20:56,100 --> 00:20:59,180
No wonder you were running for life back there.

265
00:20:59,200 --> 00:21:02,000
What? I just needed some time to muster up.

266
00:21:02,900 --> 00:21:06,420
I see. You sure took a long time, huh?

267
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:10,370
But thank you anyway.

268
00:21:15,700 --> 00:21:17,580
Just leave it there. I don’t want it.

269
00:21:19,300 --> 00:21:21,180
Just stop getting into trouble.

270
00:21:30,530 --> 00:21:31,330
Let’s go back.

271
00:22:02,730 --> 00:22:05,300
Hey, isn’t that Kaphrao?

272
00:22:05,370 --> 00:22:06,900
Come on, let’s get her!

273
00:22:07,670 --> 00:22:11,380
Ugly Kaphrao! A stray kid with no parents!

274
00:22:12,070 --> 00:22:13,540
I have Uncle Ak.

275
00:22:18,770 --> 00:22:21,530
Abandoned kid, no one wants you!

276
00:22:22,330 --> 00:22:24,870
Abandoned kid, no one wants you!

277
00:22:25,670 --> 00:22:28,000
Abandoned kid, no one wants you!

278
00:22:28,900 --> 00:22:30,700
- Abandoned kid, no one–
- [Fai]: Stop it!

279
00:22:32,130 --> 00:22:33,660
Stop bullying her!

280
00:22:34,930 --> 00:22:36,620
Fai…

281
00:22:37,300 --> 00:22:40,780
You fool! Haven’t I told you not to be weak?

282
00:22:42,530 --> 00:22:45,100
You, second grade, stay out of this!

283
00:22:45,300 --> 00:22:46,380
No! Are you going to stop?

284
00:22:46,870 --> 00:22:47,980
No!

285
00:22:48,470 --> 00:22:51,260
Kaphroa has no father! Kaphrao has no mother!

286
00:22:51,270 --> 00:22:53,380
[Fai]: I said stop it!
[Bullies]: Kaphrao has no mother!

287
00:22:55,700 --> 00:23:05,330
Ouch!

288
00:23:06,400 --> 00:23:09,540
Ouch! Stop it! Get off me!

289
00:23:09,540 --> 00:23:11,140
Ouch!

290
00:23:14,980 --> 00:23:16,500
Come on, get up.

291
00:23:17,580 --> 00:23:18,540
Are you going to stop?

292
00:23:21,800 --> 00:23:23,300
I’ll go tell the teacher!

293
00:23:23,300 --> 00:23:25,820
Get lost, losers! You, rotten jerks!

294
00:24:31,100 --> 00:24:33,340
That’s all right. I can get up on my own.

295
00:25:08,530 --> 00:25:09,470
Why are you following me?

296
00:25:09,800 --> 00:25:11,170
Just go to your room.

297
00:25:13,470 --> 00:25:17,140
I want to make sure you won’t go out to cause any trouble again.

298
00:25:18,200 --> 00:25:19,340
Annoying.

299
00:25:20,170 --> 00:25:23,460
Why? Don’t you want to hear my pretty voice?

300
00:25:23,700 --> 00:25:26,140
I’m telling you, I used to be a singer when I was still in college.

301
00:25:28,500 --> 00:25:29,300
Ew!

302
00:25:31,530 --> 00:25:32,330
Hang on.

303
00:25:34,730 --> 00:25:35,530
What now?

304
00:25:38,400 --> 00:25:41,100
I’m sorry I said bad things to you.

305
00:25:50,900 --> 00:25:52,980
Mhm, I’m used to it.

306
00:26:04,970 --> 00:26:06,700
She can talk nicely too, huh?

307
00:26:14,870 --> 00:26:16,620
I’m really sorry.

308
00:26:34,330 --> 00:26:35,300
Miss Phrao.

309
00:26:35,300 --> 00:26:37,580
Miss Rose, good morning.

310
00:26:37,580 --> 00:26:38,660
Please don’t do that.

311
00:26:40,170 --> 00:26:41,700
You went for a jog since early morning?

312
00:26:42,530 --> 00:26:44,300
A woman should never stop glowing.

313
00:26:45,400 --> 00:26:46,200
Right.

314
00:26:47,070 --> 00:26:49,340
What will you wear to the party tonight?

315
00:26:50,500 --> 00:26:53,740
Well, I’m afraid I won’t attend it.

316
00:26:54,170 --> 00:26:54,970
Why not?

317
00:26:55,470 --> 00:26:57,460
I didn’t bring any party dress with me.

318
00:26:58,870 --> 00:27:02,780
That’s all right. You can wear mine–I’ve brought lots of them.

319
00:27:03,700 --> 00:27:07,500
Oh, I’d rather not. I…I…

320
00:27:08,140 --> 00:27:10,780
Don’t worry. Just come to my room, okay?

321
00:27:10,780 --> 00:27:14,020
I’ll make you the most beautiful woman tonight.

322
00:27:15,130 --> 00:27:16,270
You can’t be serious.

323
00:27:17,000 --> 00:27:17,800
I am!

324
00:27:21,400 --> 00:27:23,780
[Fai]: She’s so ugly–not even a bit cute.

325
00:27:23,780 --> 00:27:27,780
[Fai]: She loves to fix things with her fists. Who, in their right mind, would like her?

326
00:27:35,400 --> 00:27:36,800
I’m not that pretty.

327
00:27:39,500 --> 00:27:41,370
Are you still thinking about last night?

328
00:27:44,130 --> 00:27:46,200
Please ignore what Fai said.

329
00:27:46,800 --> 00:27:50,070
I’ll make her take back every single word.

330
00:27:57,300 --> 00:27:59,770
Please trust me. It’ll be great.

331
00:28:18,820 --> 00:28:21,580
♫But then who are you?♫

332
00:28:21,580 --> 00:28:25,500
♫To make my heart keep fluttering♫

333
00:28:25,500 --> 00:28:28,140
♫Please tell me♫

334
00:28:28,140 --> 00:28:31,300
♫What’s happening with my heart?♫

335
00:28:31,300 --> 00:28:34,540
♫It can’t be, why am I feeling this?♫

336
00:28:34,540 --> 00:28:37,700
♫Oh, my heart is pounding so fast♫

337
00:28:37,700 --> 00:28:40,860
♫Time freezes whenever I see you♫

338
00:28:40,860 --> 00:28:44,180
♫I wonder why every time you smile♫

339
00:28:44,180 --> 00:28:47,420
♫Something in your eyes make me go weak♫

340
00:28:47,420 --> 00:28:50,620
♫Oh no, this is real–it’s not a dream♫

341
00:28:50,620 --> 00:28:53,500
♫Or is the love that people are saying...♫

342
00:28:53,780 --> 00:28:55,260
♫Is it you?♫

343
00:28:55,500 --> 00:28:56,300
It’s done.

344
00:29:00,300 --> 00:29:03,020
Wow! You look completely different.

345
00:29:05,900 --> 00:29:07,380
Isn’t it too heavy?

346
00:29:08,000 --> 00:29:08,870
It’s beautiful.

347
00:29:11,900 --> 00:29:15,370
I usually work in the mine or plantation.

348
00:29:16,000 --> 00:29:18,260
I don’t know who I should look pretty for.

349
00:29:20,700 --> 00:29:23,100
It’s for yourself. No need to do it for anyone.

350
00:29:23,100 --> 00:29:28,180
So that when we look at ourselves in the mirror, we could be proud of our own beauty from inside out.

351
00:29:45,370 --> 00:29:46,170
Do you like it?

352
00:29:47,170 --> 00:29:47,970
Yes.

353
00:29:48,930 --> 00:29:49,940
So pretty.

354
00:29:51,380 --> 00:29:53,100
[LADARA Resort & Spa]

355
00:30:05,530 --> 00:30:10,020
Listen, Rose gave Phrao her best dress and it looks so pretty on her!

356
00:30:10,020 --> 00:30:14,780
But maybe she’s never curled her hair before. She looks quite stiff and nervous.

357
00:30:14,780 --> 00:30:16,860
But, overall, she looks really pretty.

358
00:30:16,860 --> 00:30:20,420
Ha! I guess Boss Rose must be having a headache by now.

359
00:30:20,470 --> 00:30:23,100
Why in the world would she try to give that monkey a makeover?

360
00:30:23,700 --> 00:30:25,670
Hey, what’s so bad about Phrao?

361
00:30:25,930 --> 00:30:27,700
I think she’s cute for her age.

362
00:30:29,130 --> 00:30:34,570
That’s it, Din. I’m going to tell Boss Rose you compliment other girls.

363
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:38,980
What? Why can’t I compliment her? She’s really cute.

364
00:30:38,980 --> 00:30:41,980
I sent Lom a picture of her and she also said Phrao is cute.

365
00:30:42,000 --> 00:30:45,900
That’s because you guys are getting old and have bad eyesights.

366
00:30:48,130 --> 00:30:49,820
How the heck can you find her cute?

367
00:30:51,930 --> 00:30:52,730
I’m going nuts!

368
00:30:56,300 --> 00:30:58,730
Yeah, she’s not cute.

369
00:30:59,900 --> 00:31:00,980
There! You see?

370
00:31:01,540 --> 00:31:03,300
Even Nam agrees with me this time.

371
00:31:05,600 --> 00:31:06,500
But she’s beautiful.

372
00:32:24,940 --> 00:32:29,780
Your mouth is so wide open a bunch of flies can get in.

373
00:32:32,370 --> 00:32:33,170
Close it.

374
00:32:39,700 --> 00:32:41,400
Isn’t she pretty, Fai?

375
00:32:42,470 --> 00:32:43,270
Ye–

376
00:32:45,470 --> 00:32:46,470
She’s just okay.

377
00:32:48,400 --> 00:32:49,530
Not that pretty.

378
00:32:56,000 --> 00:32:57,970
I’ll go find something to eat first.

379
00:33:08,370 --> 00:33:10,530
If you call a girl that pretty ‘just okay’,

380
00:33:11,370 --> 00:33:14,600
I guess your type is probably as high as the moon.

381
00:33:17,070 --> 00:33:22,700
But I think she looks so beautiful tonight. Look at her.

382
00:33:24,530 --> 00:33:28,300
Trust me, some guys will be lining up to talk to her soon.

383
00:33:35,200 --> 00:33:36,100
Good evening.

384
00:33:36,940 --> 00:33:39,540
Sorry for intruding, but are you here alone?

385
00:33:40,770 --> 00:33:42,670
Look what I just said.

386
00:33:47,330 --> 00:33:49,470
I’ll just…excuse myself then.

387
00:34:01,370 --> 00:34:03,130
Would you like to join me at the table?

388
00:34:03,900 --> 00:34:04,870
Maybe not.

389
00:34:27,130 --> 00:34:28,699
Why are you following me?

390
00:34:29,730 --> 00:34:33,060
What? Who’s following you? I’m here to get something to eat too.

391
00:34:33,620 --> 00:34:35,540
Don’t be so full of yourself.

392
00:34:37,370 --> 00:34:40,469
I’ll go get some air outside. Don’t follow me.

393
00:34:55,370 --> 00:35:00,800
Look at her. She said she doesn’t care but she keeps following her like a puppy.

394
00:35:01,570 --> 00:35:05,340
Should’ve given her head a shake, so she’d finally come to her senses.

395
00:35:05,700 --> 00:35:07,700
She definitely needs it.

396
00:35:09,330 --> 00:35:14,930
But maybe, having Miss Phrao by her side might help make her life better.

397
00:35:25,100 --> 00:35:28,470
Coming out for air, huh? Why walking barefoot like you’re filming for an MV?

398
00:35:28,800 --> 00:35:31,300
Why the hell would you follow me? Just go talk to your sisters.

399
00:35:31,570 --> 00:35:32,970
No, it’s too crowded there.

400
00:35:33,800 --> 00:35:37,000
Look, if you’re going to pick a fight with me again–just go back inside.

401
00:35:43,130 --> 00:35:44,170
Why are you staring at me?

402
00:35:46,370 --> 00:35:48,140
Do you have eyes on your head?

403
00:35:49,170 --> 00:35:49,970
No.

404
00:35:52,400 --> 00:35:55,470
See? Definitely a death stare.

405
00:35:57,570 --> 00:35:59,570
You’re a nuisance–always causing trouble.

406
00:36:00,600 --> 00:36:02,100
That’s why you hate me, isn’t it?

407
00:36:05,600 --> 00:36:10,400
If you hate me, why don’t we just mind our own business? Why keep following me around just to pick a fight?

408
00:36:12,530 --> 00:36:14,300
Who said I hate you?

409
00:36:15,530 --> 00:36:19,020
You did, both through your words and actions.

410
00:36:20,540 --> 00:36:23,660
Even now when we’re talking, you can’t stand looking at me.

411
00:36:27,270 --> 00:36:28,970
When did I tell you that I hate you?

412
00:36:29,370 --> 00:36:31,400
When we were young, you always said it.

413
00:36:33,300 --> 00:36:35,170
And when was the last time I said it?

414
00:36:39,200 --> 00:36:44,300
ut you can believe it all you like since you hate me too. We’re even then.

415
00:36:46,170 --> 00:36:50,140
I actually don’t hate you–I just don’t like you.

416
00:36:50,870 --> 00:36:51,870
How’s that different?

417
00:36:52,100 --> 00:36:56,260
There! That’s what I don’t like–always ready to explode like a walking fireball.

418
00:36:56,470 --> 00:37:00,400
Then, do you expect me to sit back and laugh at it when someone says they don’t like me?

419
00:37:00,600 --> 00:37:02,940
If you want them to like you, then try to be nice.

420
00:37:02,940 --> 00:37:07,100
If you can quit being so hot-tempered and headstrong, and try to be more mature;

421
00:37:08,970 --> 00:37:12,970
I’m sure someone will definitely be interested in you.

422
00:37:19,930 --> 00:37:21,730
It’s not like I want anyone to be interested in me.

423
00:37:53,200 --> 00:37:53,980
Phrao!

424
00:37:54,540 --> 00:37:55,740
Are you Kaphrao?

425
00:37:58,200 --> 00:37:59,000
Nod!

426
00:37:59,300 --> 00:38:00,100
[Squealing with joy]

427
00:38:03,270 --> 00:38:04,170
[Kaphrao]: I miss you!

428
00:38:06,470 --> 00:38:08,330
[Nod]: Phrao! Never thought I’d see you here!

429
00:38:08,530 --> 00:38:10,620
[Kaphrao]: Yeah! I’m so happy!

430
00:38:22,570 --> 00:38:24,800
This is Fai, my boss.

431
00:38:28,870 --> 00:38:30,570
This is Nod, my close friend.

432
00:38:31,700 --> 00:38:32,500
Hello.

433
00:38:33,600 --> 00:38:34,400
Hello.

434
00:38:36,460 --> 00:38:38,700
[Kaphrao]: Aww, miss you so much!

435
00:38:39,470 --> 00:38:40,700
[Nod]: You look so skinny.

436
00:38:40,970 --> 00:38:41,770
[Kaphrao]: Really?
- [Nod]: Have you lost weight?

437
00:38:41,870 --> 00:38:43,270
[Nod]: Aww, why? Are you on a diet?

438
00:38:43,600 --> 00:38:45,140
You have to treat me to a meal then.

439
00:38:45,140 --> 00:38:46,500
Sure, what do you want to eat?

440
00:38:46,900 --> 00:38:47,780
Pork leg!

441
00:38:49,130 --> 00:38:50,000
Whatever you say!

442
00:38:54,500 --> 00:38:56,900
So, we haven’t met since we graduated, right?

443
00:38:57,370 --> 00:39:00,100
That’s because you went to study abroad.

444
00:39:00,730 --> 00:39:02,730
So, how come you’re invited to the party too?

445
00:39:03,270 --> 00:39:06,500
My uncle also owns a hotel, so he and Miss Nam know each other.

446
00:39:06,870 --> 00:39:08,530
That’s why she invited us.

447
00:39:09,100 --> 00:39:10,470
What about you?

448
00:39:11,070 --> 00:39:13,000
Fai is Miss Nam’s cousin.

449
00:39:13,170 --> 00:39:15,600
I’m working with her in Surat Thani, so I just tag along here.

450
00:39:16,200 --> 00:39:18,670
I see. So, you’ve moved to Surat.

451
00:39:19,130 --> 00:39:21,530
That’s why none of our friends have heard from you.

452
00:39:21,800 --> 00:39:23,400
That’s because I don’t do social media.

453
00:39:23,670 --> 00:39:26,940
I also got a new number so I’ve lost all the contacts and didn’t call anyone.

454
00:39:27,300 --> 00:39:31,000
I thought so. It was just the two of us back then, remember?

455
00:39:31,500 --> 00:39:32,300
Yeah.

456
00:39:34,130 --> 00:39:36,070
Looks like you two are really close, huh?

457
00:39:37,770 --> 00:39:38,900
Absolutely!

458
00:39:39,530 --> 00:39:41,800
We were inseparable back then, right?

459
00:39:42,000 --> 00:39:42,800
Yes.

460
00:39:42,900 --> 00:39:46,620
We played together, studied together, ate together, and even shared the same bed.

461
00:39:48,130 --> 00:39:50,900
Our teachers often called us the twins of Siam.

462
00:39:50,970 --> 00:39:52,600
We even went to the toilet together.

463
00:39:53,170 --> 00:39:55,940
Oh, and we used to sneak out at night and fall off the dorm too.

464
00:39:55,940 --> 00:39:58,820
[Kaphrao]: Nod, don’t! That’s TMI.
- [Nod]: Back then, you were–

465
00:39:58,820 --> 00:40:01,660
[Kaphrao]: Stop it, Nod.
[Nod]: Why? It’s so funny.

466
00:40:01,660 --> 00:40:03,940
I’m tired. I’m going back to my room.

467
00:40:05,870 --> 00:40:07,900
Go then. Why are you telling me?

468
00:40:08,070 --> 00:40:10,700
Dad told me to look after you. How could I leave you here alone?

469
00:40:10,940 --> 00:40:13,460
What if anything happens like last night?

470
00:40:15,400 --> 00:40:17,200
If I’m leaving, you have to come with me.

471
00:40:18,000 --> 00:40:19,570
But I still want to catch up with my friend here.

472
00:40:20,130 --> 00:40:21,070
But I need to sleep!

473
00:40:21,400 --> 00:40:22,370
Then, leave!

474
00:40:23,100 --> 00:40:24,600
It’s all right, Phrao.

475
00:40:25,400 --> 00:40:27,530
If she wants you to go back with her,

476
00:40:30,100 --> 00:40:32,900
why don’t we go talk in your room after this?

477
00:40:33,270 --> 00:40:34,100
Sure, that’s great!

478
00:40:35,800 --> 00:40:37,570
You can just come with me then.

479
00:40:37,900 --> 00:40:42,770
Deal! We’ll spend all night catching up and reminiscing on our good old days.

480
00:40:43,000 --> 00:40:44,660
Let’s go then, so we’ll have more time.

481
00:40:44,660 --> 00:40:45,220
Okay.

482
00:40:45,400 --> 00:40:47,900
I have so many things to tell you.

483
00:40:52,600 --> 00:40:53,730
They’re sharing a bed?

484
00:41:24,670 --> 00:41:27,060
[I’m so happy to see you, Phrao.]

485
00:41:29,000 --> 00:41:30,670
[I need to tell you something.]

486
00:41:31,530 --> 00:41:32,330
[What is it?]

487
00:41:34,500 --> 00:41:35,770
[I really miss you.]

488
00:41:48,340 --> 00:41:52,200
[Nod…]

489
00:41:54,060 --> 00:41:55,420
Shit!

490
00:42:30,100 --> 00:42:31,780
[Giggling]

491
00:43:02,500 --> 00:43:03,730
Why are you nodding off here?

492
00:43:05,370 --> 00:43:06,730
Waiting for you, of course.

493
00:43:07,600 --> 00:43:08,400
Why?

494
00:43:10,070 --> 00:43:12,200
So…we can walk to the car together.

495
00:43:15,530 --> 00:43:19,820
Hold on. Where’s your friend?

496
00:43:21,570 --> 00:43:23,000
Already left since last night.

497
00:43:26,300 --> 00:43:27,530
Better be gone for good.

498
00:43:28,370 --> 00:43:29,170
What was that?

499
00:43:30,770 --> 00:43:33,380
Nothing. Let’s go.

500
00:43:40,670 --> 00:43:41,660
Nod!

501
00:43:42,780 --> 00:43:45,620
Are you leaving? I’m here to see you off.

502
00:43:47,870 --> 00:43:48,930
Come, let me help.

503
00:43:49,070 --> 00:43:49,800
Oh, it’s all right.

504
00:43:49,800 --> 00:43:51,130
That’s fine. It’s nothing.

505
00:43:51,600 --> 00:43:52,400
Thank you.

506
00:43:52,900 --> 00:43:54,100
You’re the sweetest!

507
00:43:55,270 --> 00:43:56,460
What do you want to eat?

508
00:43:57,570 --> 00:43:58,670
[Mocking] You’re the sweetest!

509
00:43:59,370 --> 00:44:00,170
What do you want to eat?

510
00:44:14,000 --> 00:44:19,930
Young Master, the Big Boss wants you both to go see him. He needs to talk to you about something.

511
00:44:20,570 --> 00:44:22,730
Can you tell Dad we’ll go talk to him tomorrow?

512
00:44:23,100 --> 00:44:24,300
I’m so exhausted from the trip.

513
00:44:24,530 --> 00:44:27,940
This Gremlin’s driving skill completely sucks–I could barely sleep.

514
00:44:28,200 --> 00:44:29,530
Why didn’t you drive it yourself?

515
00:44:30,600 --> 00:44:31,400
It’s all right.

516
00:44:31,500 --> 00:44:32,300
I’m not tired.

517
00:44:32,300 --> 00:44:33,100
I can go see him now.

518
00:44:34,900 --> 00:44:36,100
Hold it right there!

519
00:44:36,380 --> 00:44:38,300
Suddenly wagging your tail to suck up to him, huh?

520
00:44:38,400 --> 00:44:40,170
If you don’t want to go, then stay here. I’ll go.

521
00:44:41,170 --> 00:44:43,470
Are you finding an excuse to be alone with my dad?

522
00:44:44,780 --> 00:44:45,980
B.N.R!

523
00:44:47,070 --> 00:44:47,770
What?

524
00:44:47,770 --> 00:44:48,940
Bloody Nerve-Racking!

525
00:44:49,670 --> 00:44:51,100
Then stop flirting around.

526
00:44:51,200 --> 00:44:52,340
Save your stinking breath!

527
00:44:52,500 --> 00:44:54,770
Just go to bed if you’re sleepy, so that you won’t lash out on me.

528
00:44:54,930 --> 00:44:56,300
I’ll only leave if you do.

529
00:44:56,300 --> 00:44:56,900
You!

530
00:44:56,900 --> 00:45:01,460
All right then, why don’t you go talk to him tomorrow? I’ll let the Master know.

531
00:45:03,470 --> 00:45:07,580
Okay. Please walk her home and make sure she gets in the house.

532
00:45:07,580 --> 00:45:11,020
Don’t let her sneak out to seduce my dad.

533
00:45:17,670 --> 00:45:20,470
Go then. I’ll wait until you’re out of my sight.

534
00:45:24,170 --> 00:45:25,540
Ouch! That was harsh.

535
00:45:25,540 --> 00:45:26,600
Let me help you, Miss.

536
00:45:27,770 --> 00:45:28,570
Please excuse me.

537
00:45:36,530 --> 00:45:37,400
Whose bag is this?

538
00:45:37,670 --> 00:45:38,470
Mine.

539
00:45:39,070 --> 00:45:40,000
Here you go, Young Master.

540
00:45:48,400 --> 00:45:49,200
Let’s go.

541
00:45:52,870 --> 00:45:53,670
What’s wrong?

542
00:46:25,530 --> 00:46:27,000
I’m home n–

543
00:46:36,370 --> 00:46:38,580
Aww, Auntie, Auntie, Auntie, Auntie!

544
00:46:38,580 --> 00:46:40,180
My lovely Auntie.

545
00:46:41,180 --> 00:46:44,060
Talk to me first, Pretty Lady.

546
00:46:48,300 --> 00:46:51,900
Hmm, are you still mad at me?

547
00:46:54,100 --> 00:46:58,340
Do you still care? You hardly listen to me these days.

548
00:46:59,570 --> 00:47:03,070
Who told you that? I’ll always be your good girl, Auntie.

549
00:47:05,600 --> 00:47:07,500
Then, why didn’t you listen to me this time?

550
00:47:09,400 --> 00:47:10,970
Why did you take that girl with you?

551
00:47:13,200 --> 00:47:14,900
Because Dad made me do it.

552
00:47:16,600 --> 00:47:19,070
You usually never listen to whatever he says.

553
00:47:20,900 --> 00:47:22,980
I’m following your advice.

554
00:47:22,980 --> 00:47:28,300
You told me to keep an eye on her, and never leave her alone with Dad.

555
00:47:28,580 --> 00:47:29,620
Remember?

556
00:47:30,200 --> 00:47:32,860
But, right now, it’s different.

557
00:47:32,860 --> 00:47:38,980
What if that girl changes her mind and tries to get her hands on you instead? What would you do?

558
00:47:39,900 --> 00:47:42,820
Come on, Auntie. Where did you get that idea from?

559
00:47:43,380 --> 00:47:46,220
That’s impossible. She hates me to her guts.

560
00:47:47,020 --> 00:47:48,100
So funny.

561
00:47:50,530 --> 00:47:55,130
Then, promise me you’ll never fall for her.

562
00:47:57,540 --> 00:48:04,700
Yes, I’ll never fall for anyone. I’ll stay with you forever.

563
00:48:05,220 --> 00:48:08,020
I’ll let you take care of me until I’m old, okay?

564
00:48:08,580 --> 00:48:10,300
Can you live until then?

565
00:48:12,820 --> 00:48:14,860
Come, let’s go to sleep. It’s late.

566
00:48:17,900 --> 00:48:21,500
I was so exhausted earlier but seeing you just freshen me up.

567
00:48:21,500 --> 00:48:25,340
Give me a peck. Come on, let’s go.

568
00:48:28,700 --> 00:48:30,300
Can I sleep in your room tonight?

569
00:48:30,660 --> 00:48:31,340
Mhm.

570
00:48:37,670 --> 00:48:38,470
Please come in.

571
00:48:38,570 --> 00:48:40,780
By the way, I forgot to ask.

572
00:48:41,260 --> 00:48:44,460
How was the trip with Young Master? Did you enjoy it?

573
00:48:44,740 --> 00:48:47,180
You two didn’t fight all the way home, did you?

574
00:48:48,600 --> 00:48:51,940
You wish. It’s lucky we got back safely.

575
00:48:51,940 --> 00:48:55,980
Oh, was it that bad? Quite disappointing though.

576
00:48:56,070 --> 00:49:00,660
I thought you and Young Master would finally become close again, just like the old days.

577
00:49:02,170 --> 00:49:03,770
That will never happen, Uncle Yod.

578
00:49:04,730 --> 00:49:05,770
Well, who knows?

579
00:49:07,000 --> 00:49:09,420
Young Master usually doesn’t like to be with anyone except Miss Panee.

580
00:49:10,020 --> 00:49:14,900
But after you came here, she’s been hanging out with you quite often lately.

581
00:49:14,900 --> 00:49:21,100
The only reason she agrees to hang out with me is because she wants to keep an eye on me and nitpick me on everything I do!

582
00:49:26,200 --> 00:49:26,740
So…

583
00:49:27,540 --> 00:49:31,660
Why would Uncle want me to go see him tomorrow?

584
00:49:31,800 --> 00:49:34,070
I also don’t have the faintest idea.

585
00:49:35,930 --> 00:49:41,700
I hope he won’t assign me to a job that would put me through another hell with that Buff–Fai again.

586
00:49:45,170 --> 00:49:47,800
I also hope it won’t be like that.

587
00:49:49,700 --> 00:49:50,500
I’m leaving then.

588
00:49:51,270 --> 00:49:52,930
Thank you so much, Uncle Yod.

589
00:49:53,270 --> 00:49:54,700
- Have a nice evening.
- Yes.

590
00:50:13,930 --> 00:50:19,060
Do you remember that show where they interviewed Miss Blew about her life while she was staying on our island?

591
00:50:19,420 --> 00:50:23,380
After it aired, many people have expressed interest in visiting there.

592
00:50:24,770 --> 00:50:28,600
Yeah, Nam also mentioned it to me when I met her in Hua Hin.

593
00:50:29,570 --> 00:50:32,860
That’s why I plan to build some accommodations there,

594
00:50:33,140 --> 00:50:36,700
and turn our island into an ecotourism attraction.

595
00:50:37,300 --> 00:50:42,020
This is the plan I’ve written in detail.

596
00:50:42,270 --> 00:50:46,900
I want you and Kaphrao to go there to see if there’s anything else we could improve.

597
00:50:48,730 --> 00:50:49,600
Me and Kaphrao?

598
00:50:50,170 --> 00:50:50,970
Yes.

599
00:50:51,870 --> 00:50:53,600
What does that have to do with her?

600
00:50:54,370 --> 00:50:55,260
Well,

601
00:50:56,060 --> 00:51:00,540
I want you and Kaphrao to look after this project together.

602
00:51:01,060 --> 00:51:06,980
I already told Boonsong. You can go talk to him tomorrow, okay?

603
00:51:44,370 --> 00:51:47,400
Can’t you tell the time? I said let’s meet at 7.

604
00:51:50,600 --> 00:51:54,100
It’s now 6.55–that’s not 7 yet.

605
00:51:55,100 --> 00:51:56,980
You’re here early. Can’t blame me.

606
00:51:57,300 --> 00:51:59,670
Save your excuses. My legs are growing roots here.

607
00:51:59,770 --> 00:52:00,580
Really? Where?

608
00:52:01,220 --> 00:52:02,940
I don’t see a single root here.

609
00:52:02,940 --> 00:52:04,070
It can almost strangle your neck.

610
00:52:04,200 --> 00:52:05,780
Aww, where is it? So scary!

611
00:52:05,780 --> 00:52:06,740
Guinea Pig!

612
00:52:06,800 --> 00:52:08,500
What? You started it first.

613
00:52:10,100 --> 00:52:10,900
Get in the car.

614
00:52:13,530 --> 00:52:14,600
What? Have a problem?

615
00:52:25,930 --> 00:52:27,570
[Fai]: Hey, I’m not driving. We’re not driving there.

616
00:52:27,730 --> 00:52:29,400
[Kaphrao]: Fine, then don’t. It’s not like I want you to go.

617
00:52:29,570 --> 00:52:31,570
[Fai]: Good, close the door then.
- [Kaphrao]: Okay!

618
00:52:31,870 --> 00:52:32,580
Bye!

619
00:52:33,180 --> 00:52:33,980
Don’t come out then.

620
00:52:34,340 --> 00:52:37,220
Oh, why are you sweating?

621
00:52:38,970 --> 00:52:40,130
Are you sweating?

622
00:52:56,330 --> 00:52:57,870
I’ll go to the loo then.

623
00:53:03,130 --> 00:53:05,200
[Staff]: Hello, what petrol would you like?

624
00:53:05,370 --> 00:53:06,870
Diesel, fill up the tank please.

625
00:53:08,900 --> 00:53:09,700
What is it?

626
00:53:11,300 --> 00:53:13,100
Shit!

627
00:53:13,870 --> 00:53:14,900
I’m so sorry.

628
00:53:15,500 --> 00:53:21,460
Young Master, I really miss my parents so I decided to sneak into your car.

629
00:53:22,100 --> 00:53:24,940
It’s not a big deal at all, you could’ve just asked her nicely, Bua.

630
00:53:26,260 --> 00:53:30,380
Well, I…I was afraid you mightn’t let me come with you.

631
00:53:31,200 --> 00:53:33,660
Your Young Master is probably not that heartless.

632
00:53:34,220 --> 00:53:35,260
Right?

633
00:53:39,500 --> 00:53:41,580
Young Master, please let me go with you too.

634
00:53:41,580 --> 00:53:44,460
I promise I’ll behave. Please!

635
00:53:44,460 --> 00:53:46,580
Please, Young Master! Please…let me go with you too.

636
00:53:46,580 --> 00:53:48,860
Please, please, please! Let me go with you.

637
00:53:48,860 --> 00:53:50,340
[Bua]: Please, please, please!
[Fai]: Okay, fine!

638
00:53:50,770 --> 00:53:52,530
We’ve already come this far, I guess I don’t have a choice.

639
00:53:52,770 --> 00:53:54,400
I wouldn’t go all the way back just to drop you off.

640
00:53:54,600 --> 00:53:56,970
Aww, Young Master, you’re the best indeed!

641
00:53:57,170 --> 00:53:58,860
Can I go sit in the car then?

642
00:53:58,860 --> 00:54:01,820
It’s bloody hot up here. You hardly stop by anywhere.

643
00:54:01,900 --> 00:54:02,700
Huh, my fault then?

644
00:54:02,800 --> 00:54:03,600
Wait for me too.

645
00:54:08,130 --> 00:54:09,220
I’m coming.

646
00:54:09,370 --> 00:54:10,660
How could you stand the heat?

647
00:54:10,670 --> 00:54:11,470
Right?

648
00:54:11,800 --> 00:54:13,130
I don’t get it either.

649
00:54:15,000 --> 00:54:16,970
Hi, everyone! Hello, there!

650
00:54:17,730 --> 00:54:21,180
Thank you so much for watching me LIVE today.

651
00:54:21,180 --> 00:54:27,820
Wow, you guys just keep flooding in the minute I come online–as if you’ve been waiting for this moment.

652
00:54:27,820 --> 00:54:32,300
Please don’t forget to click LIKE and SHARE for me, and SUBSCRIBE too.

653
00:54:32,300 --> 00:54:38,900
Thanks for watching me LIVE today. I’ve come on land to try the coffee at a new coffee shop.

654
00:54:42,300 --> 00:54:49,140
Wow! It’s really good. Maybe I should open a branch on the island.

655
00:54:49,200 --> 00:54:52,460
Just comment if you have any idea about it.

656
00:54:52,900 --> 00:54:54,540
- Yeah, okay?
- [Bua]: Dad!

657
00:54:55,600 --> 00:54:56,400
Dad!

658
00:54:56,470 --> 00:54:58,020
- Bua?
- Daddy! I miss you so much!

659
00:54:59,070 --> 00:55:01,700
All right, all right. I know it. So…

660
00:55:01,940 --> 00:55:04,580
Don’t you have to work today? Why are you here?

661
00:55:04,580 --> 00:55:05,660
Are you skipping work?

662
00:55:05,700 --> 00:55:07,800
Geez, Dad. I’ve already asked Young Master and she agreed.

663
00:55:07,970 --> 00:55:10,260
[Bua]: Aww, Dad. Miss you!
[Boonsong]: Young Master is generous.

664
00:55:10,300 --> 00:55:11,600
Are you sure you’ve asked?

665
00:55:15,900 --> 00:55:16,770
Hello, Young Master.

666
00:55:16,970 --> 00:55:17,770
Hello.

667
00:55:21,870 --> 00:55:25,470
This is Kaphrao, an assistant Dad has sent to help me.

668
00:55:29,300 --> 00:55:33,330
Kaphrao, this is Uncle Boonsong–the head of Fisherman’s Village on my dad’s island.

669
00:55:33,700 --> 00:55:35,500
And he’s also my father.

670
00:55:36,730 --> 00:55:37,900
Hello, Uncle Boonsong.

671
00:55:38,200 --> 00:55:39,670
Hello, Miss Kaphrao.

672
00:55:41,260 --> 00:55:45,500
Dad, why don’t we go talk over there instead? It’s hot here.

673
00:55:45,570 --> 00:55:46,700
Yeah, it’s quite hot here.

674
00:55:46,700 --> 00:55:48,380
Right? Come on then. Let’s go over there.

675
00:55:48,400 --> 00:55:50,540
Let’s go. Oh, I’m still on LIVE!

676
00:55:50,540 --> 00:55:52,020
[Bua]: Oh, okay.
[Boonsong]: That’s it for today then.

677
00:55:52,020 --> 00:55:54,380
Say bye, everyone! Bye!

678
00:55:54,380 --> 00:55:56,780
I’ll see you later.

679
00:55:57,070 --> 00:55:58,100
You’re addicted to it now.

680
00:55:58,980 --> 00:55:59,740
Let’s go.

681
00:55:59,740 --> 00:56:00,860
I have nothing to do.

682
00:56:01,500 --> 00:56:03,380
Aww, miss you so much!

683
00:56:03,870 --> 00:56:06,270
[Boonsong]: If it’s still hot there, should we go talk in the water then?

684
00:56:06,270 --> 00:56:08,400
[Bua]: No! Let’s not do that.

685
00:56:10,100 --> 00:56:11,860
Here, please have a look at it first.

686
00:56:11,870 --> 00:56:12,820
Thank you.

687
00:56:13,670 --> 00:56:18,740
Dad wants to know if you think it’s possible to open a small homestay on the island,

688
00:56:18,740 --> 00:56:22,620
promote ecotourism there, and have the villagers run everything by themselves.

689
00:56:24,800 --> 00:56:31,300
I think if the number of tourists is quite small, the villagers can definitely manage.

690
00:56:31,780 --> 00:56:34,020
Just like when Miss Lom and Miss Blew stayed there.

691
00:56:39,000 --> 00:56:41,300
We can start off with just a few cottages first.

692
00:56:41,900 --> 00:56:45,740
Maybe, we shouldn’t focus on making profits, but rather creating income for the villagers.

693
00:56:45,770 --> 00:56:47,000
What do you think?

694
00:56:47,770 --> 00:56:49,260
That’s wonderful then.

695
00:56:49,570 --> 00:56:52,820
I’ll go talk to the villagers and explain the idea to them.

696
00:56:54,470 --> 00:56:57,540
By the way, do you need to go to the island? If so, I’ll go get the boat ready.

697
00:57:00,670 --> 00:57:01,620
That’s all right.

698
00:57:02,900 --> 00:57:05,860
I go there quite often. I already have an idea what needs to be done here.

699
00:57:07,140 --> 00:57:07,660
Yes.

700
00:57:07,970 --> 00:57:12,460
Too bad then. I thought you’d take Miss Phrao to see the island.

701
00:57:12,460 --> 00:57:14,500
So that she’d know what it’s like there.

702
00:57:15,670 --> 00:57:17,370
You’ve never been there, Miss Phrao?

703
00:57:18,000 --> 00:57:20,200
No. I really want to go there.

704
00:57:23,800 --> 00:57:25,020
Why would you want to go there?

705
00:57:25,980 --> 00:57:29,140
There’s no facilities on the island and it’s not as convenient as you think.

706
00:57:29,140 --> 00:57:32,860
I guarantee if you go there, you’ll get bored the moment your feet touch the sand.

707
00:57:33,270 --> 00:57:38,060
But Uncle has assigned me to this project, so I’m supposed to go inspect the area.

708
00:57:38,100 --> 00:57:39,740
Otherwise, how would you expect me to work?

709
00:57:42,870 --> 00:57:43,930
I want to go there!

710
00:57:44,670 --> 00:57:46,500
But Young Master won’t be coming with us today.

711
00:57:47,870 --> 00:57:51,860
That’s fine. I can go with Bua.

712
00:57:54,060 --> 00:57:55,700
Well, then…

713
00:57:57,200 --> 00:57:58,820
You’re welcome.

714
00:58:10,730 --> 00:58:11,770
[Bua]: How is it, Dad? Sweet?

715
00:58:12,930 --> 00:58:14,660
[Boonsong]: Yeah, bittersweet.
- [Bua]: I see.

716
00:58:42,750 --> 00:58:44,520
[Next Episode]
Wow!

717
00:58:44,520 --> 00:58:47,350
[Fai]: This place holds a lot of memories between Lom and Miss Blew.

718
00:58:47,350 --> 00:58:49,850
Is there anything else that we can use as a selling point?

719
00:58:50,250 --> 00:58:51,450
We have pink shells here.

720
00:58:51,450 --> 00:58:54,450
If you find it, you’ll get to make a wish.

721
00:58:55,780 --> 00:58:57,020
What the hell?

722
00:58:58,480 --> 00:58:59,450
There’s a cave over there. Let’s go!

723
00:58:59,450 --> 00:59:01,520
What? Suddenly pouring down like this?

724
00:59:01,520 --> 00:59:04,980
When I want to be secluded, I’d either set up a tent somewhere on the island or sleep in this cave.

725
00:59:04,980 --> 00:59:06,950
You think you’re a hermit or what?

726
00:59:06,950 --> 00:59:08,180
It’s called being Indie*. (*Independent)

727
00:59:08,180 --> 00:59:11,150
What? Does that mean we won’t be able to leave until tomorrow?

728
00:59:11,150 --> 00:59:14,920
If you’re not going to sleep, stay up and keep watch until morning then.

729
00:59:18,550 --> 00:59:19,620
[Miming] Go downstairs.

730
00:59:37,780 --> 00:59:44,820
♫I still remember vividly that day when we first met♫

731
00:59:45,380 --> 00:59:51,180
♫Those memories we had together never fade away from my heart♫

732
00:59:51,540 --> 00:59:59,140
♫We might never say it out loud how we feel for each other♫

733
00:59:59,140 --> 01:00:04,900
♫But deep down we both know how we feel♫

734
01:00:04,900 --> 01:00:11,020
♫Those things in the past, I still can’t forget them♫

735
01:00:11,020 --> 01:00:17,140
♫I want to know if you’re like that too–do you also feel the same?♫

736
01:00:17,540 --> 01:00:25,100
♫I could never forget those eyes of yours♫

737
01:00:25,100 --> 01:00:31,540
♫The warmth you used to give me, I still remember it vividly♫

738
01:00:31,820 --> 01:00:38,900
♫No matter for how long, you’ll always remain in my heart♫

739
01:00:38,900 --> 01:00:49,300
♫All those years I’ve been waiting, for us to finally be together again♫

740
01:00:57,340 --> 01:01:01,220
[North Star Entertainment]

741
01:01:01,220 --> 01:01:05,220
[Flaming Chains of Love]
